{"adr":"Generate one SDK from the shared OpenAPI contract in the first screen slice; use it from both containers.\nBuild the Requests slice first so the app entry and its list/create behavior work before detail behavior is added.\nThe API server owns persistence, seeding, and API business rules; this repository owns the web client and shared contract stub.\nDo not add sign-in or other capabilities beyond the approved scope.","chosen":"single-generated-client","newDependencies":[{"name":"openapi-typescript-codegen","registry":"https://registry.npmjs.org","version":"0.29.0"}],"options":[{"id":"single-generated-client","simplest":true,"summary":"Generate the full contract SDK into lib/api in the Requests slice; both screen containers consume that SDK.","tradeoffs":"Keeps one generated client and a useful, independently verifiable Requests slice. Some detail operations are generated before TASK-3 uses them."},{"id":"per-screen-generated-clients","simplest":false,"summary":"Generate list/create operations in TASK-2 and detail/status operations in TASK-3 into separate generated SDK outputs.","tradeoffs":"Generates only the operations each slice immediately uses, but requires generator partitioning and separate generated outputs/types, increasing integration and maintenance risk."}],"protectedPathsDeclared":["package.json"],"stubs":[{"content":"export type RequestArea = \"Kitchen\" | \"Meeting room\" | \"Open desk\" | \"Washroom\" | \"Reception\";\nexport type RequestPriority = \"Low\" | \"Normal\" | \"Urgent\";\nexport type RequestStatus = \"Open\" | \"In progress\" | \"Done\";\n\nexport interface MaintenanceRequest {\n  id: number;\n  createdAt: string;\n  title: string;\n  area: RequestArea;\n  priority: RequestPriority;\n  status: RequestStatus;\n  description?: string;\n}\n\nexport interface CreateRequest {\n  title: string;\n  area: RequestArea;\n  priority: RequestPriority;\n  description?: string;\n  id?: number;\n  createdAt?: string;\n  status?: RequestStatus;\n}\n\nexport interface ChangeRequestStatus {\n  status: RequestStatus;\n}\n\nexport interface ApiError {\n  status: number;\n  body: unknown;\n}\n\nexport class DefaultService {\n  static async listRequests(_status?: RequestStatus): Promise<{ requests: MaintenanceRequest[] }> {\n    throw new Error(\"not implemented\");\n  }\n\n  static async createRequest(_requestBody: CreateRequest): Promise<MaintenanceRequest> {\n    throw new Error(\"not implemented\");\n  }\n\n  static async getRequest(_id: number): Promise<MaintenanceRequest> {\n    throw new Error(\"not implemented\");\n  }\n\n  static async changeRequestStatus(_id: number, _requestBody: ChangeRequestStatus): Promise<MaintenanceRequest> {\n    throw new Error(\"not implemented\");\n  }\n}\n","path":"lib/api/index.ts","reason":"Compile-time seam for the generated contract SDK methods and resource types used by both screen containers. Replace with SDK output generated from contracts/openapi.yaml."},{"content":"openapi: 3.0.3\ninfo:\n  title: Hive Works Maintenance Requests API\n  version: 1.0.0\n  description: Shared contract for the Hive Works maintenance web app and API.\nservers:\n  - url: /api\npaths:\n  /requests:\n    get:\n      operationId: listRequests\n      summary: List maintenance requests\n      description: Returns all requests or requests matching one supported status, newest first. Equal creation timestamps have no guaranteed relative order.\n      parameters:\n        - name: status\n          in: query\n          required: false\n          description: Optional single status filter.\n          schema:\n            $ref: '#/components/schemas/RequestStatus'\n      responses:\n        '200':\n          description: Matching requests, newest first.\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                $ref: '#/components/schemas/RequestList'\n              example:\n                requests:\n                  - { id: 1, createdAt: '2026-03-18T09:00:00Z', title: Kitchen tap leaking, area: Kitchen, priority: Urgent, status: Open }\n                  - { id: 2, createdAt: '2026-03-17T09:00:00Z', title: \"Projector won't power on\", area: Meeting room, priority: Normal, status: In progress }\n                  - { id: 3, createdAt: '2026-03-16T09:00:00Z', title: Wobbly desk B-14, area: Open desk, priority: Low, status: Open }\n                  - { id: 4, createdAt: '2026-03-15T09:00:00Z', title: Hand dryer not working, area: Washroom, priority: Normal, status: Open }\n                  - { id: 5, createdAt: '2026-03-14T09:00:00Z', title: Loose floor tile by entrance, area: Reception, priority: Urgent, status: In progress }\n                  - { id: 6, createdAt: '2026-03-12T09:00:00Z', title: Fridge door seal worn, area: Kitchen, priority: Low, status: Done }\n                  - { id: 7, createdAt: '2026-03-11T09:00:00Z', title: Whiteboard rail coming loose, area: Meeting room, priority: Normal, status: Done }\n                  - { id: 8, createdAt: '2026-03-10T09:00:00Z', title: \"Monitor arm won't hold position\", area: Open desk, priority: Low, status: Open }\n                  - { id: 9, createdAt: '2026-03-09T09:00:00Z', title: Reception door closer slams, area: Reception, priority: Urgent, status: Open }\n                  - { id: 10, createdAt: '2026-03-07T09:00:00Z', title: Washroom sink draining slowly, area: Washroom, priority: Normal, status: Done }\n                  - { id: 11, createdAt: '2026-03-06T09:00:00Z', title: Ceiling light flickering, area: Meeting room, priority: Urgent, status: In progress }\n                  - { id: 12, createdAt: '2026-03-05T09:00:00Z', title: Kitchen cabinet hinge loose, area: Kitchen, priority: Low, status: Done }\n        '400':\n          description: The status filter is unsupported or malformed.\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ErrorResponse'\n              example:\n                message: Status must be Open, In progress, or Done.\n                errors:\n                  status: [Unsupported status filter.]\n        '500':\n          description: The request list could not be loaded.\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ErrorResponse'\n              example:\n                message: Could not load requests.\n    post:\n      operationId: createRequest\n      summary: Create a maintenance request\n      description: Trims title and description before validation and storage. The API assigns id, createdAt, and Open status itself; optional caller-supplied values for those system-controlled fields are ignored. A description that is absent or blank after trimming is omitted from the resource.\n      requestBody:\n        required: true\n        content:\n          application/json:\n            schema:\n              $ref: '#/components/schemas/CreateRequest'\n            example:\n              title: Kitchen tap leaking\n              area: Kitchen\n              priority: Urgent\n              description: Water is pooling under the sink.\n      responses:\n        '201':\n          description: The created request with system-assigned fields.\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                $ref: '#/components/schemas/MaintenanceRequest'\n              example:\n                id: 13\n                createdAt: '2026-03-19T10:30:00Z'\n                title: Kitchen tap leaking\n                area: Kitchen\n                priority: Urgent\n                status: Open\n                description: Water is pooling under the sink.\n        '400':\n          description: Malformed JSON, invalid field types, missing or invalid fields, or invalid values. No request is created.\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ErrorResponse'\n              example:\n                message: Request validation failed.\n                errors:\n                  title: [Title must be 3 to 80 characters.]\n                  area: [Area is required.]\n                  description: [Description must be at most 500 characters.]\n        '500':\n          description: The request could not be created.\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ErrorResponse'\n              example:\n                message: Could not create the request.\n  /requests/{id}:\n    parameters:\n      - name: id\n        in: path\n        required: true\n        description: System-generated integer request ID.\n        schema:\n          type: integer\n          format: int64\n          minimum: 1\n    get:\n      operationId: getRequest\n      summary: Get a maintenance request\n      responses:\n        '200':\n          description: The matching request.\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                $ref: '#/components/schemas/MaintenanceRequest'\n              example:\n                id: 2\n                createdAt: '2026-03-17T09:00:00Z'\n                title: \"Projector won't power on\"\n                area: Meeting room\n                priority: Normal\n                status: In progress\n        '404':\n          description: No request has this ID.\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ErrorResponse'\n              example:\n                message: Request not found.\n        '500':\n          description: The request could not be loaded for a non-not-found reason.\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ErrorResponse'\n              example:\n                message: Could not load the request.\n  /requests/{id}/status:\n    parameters:\n      - name: id\n        in: path\n        required: true\n        description: System-generated integer request ID.\n        schema:\n          type: integer\n          format: int64\n          minimum: 1\n    patch:\n      operationId: changeRequestStatus\n      summary: Change a request's status\n      description: Only status is mutable. Allowed transitions are Open to In progress, In progress to Done, and Done to Open. Requests with immutable fields or other extra properties are rejected.\n      requestBody:\n        required: true\n        content:\n          application/json:\n            schema:\n              $ref: '#/components/schemas/ChangeRequestStatus'\n            example:\n              status: Done\n      responses:\n        '200':\n          description: The request with its updated status.\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                $ref: '#/components/schemas/MaintenanceRequest'\n              example:\n                id: 2\n                createdAt: '2026-03-17T09:00:00Z'\n                title: \"Projector won't power on\"\n                area: Meeting room\n                priority: Normal\n                status: Done\n        '400':\n          description: Unsupported status value or attempt to change an immutable field.\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ErrorResponse'\n              example:\n                message: Status must be Open, In progress, or Done; only status may be changed.\n                errors:\n                  status: [Unsupported status value.]\n        '404':\n          description: No request has this ID.\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ErrorResponse'\n              example:\n                message: Request not found.\n        '409':\n          description: The requested status transition is not allowed from the current status.\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ErrorResponse'\n              example:\n                message: This status transition is not allowed.\n        '500':\n          description: The status could not be updated.\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ErrorResponse'\n              example:\n                message: Could not update the request.\ncomponents:\n  schemas:\n    RequestArea:\n      type: string\n      enum: [Kitchen, Meeting room, Open desk, Washroom, Reception]\n    RequestPriority:\n      type: string\n      enum: [Low, Normal, Urgent]\n    RequestStatus:\n      type: string\n      enum: [Open, In progress, Done]\n    MaintenanceRequest:\n      type: object\n      additionalProperties: false\n      required: [id, createdAt, title, area, priority, status]\n      properties:\n        id:\n          type: integer\n          format: int64\n          minimum: 1\n          description: System-generated request ID.\n        createdAt:\n          type: string\n          format: date-time\n          description: System-generated UTC timestamp.\n        title:\n          type: string\n          minLength: 3\n          maxLength: 80\n        area:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/RequestArea'\n        priority:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/RequestPriority'\n        status:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/RequestStatus'\n        description:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 500\n    CreateRequest:\n      type: object\n      additionalProperties: false\n      required: [title, area, priority]\n      description: Title and description are trimmed before validation and storage. Optional id, createdAt, or status inputs are ignored and replaced by system values.\n      properties:\n        title:\n          type: string\n          minLength: 3\n          maxLength: 80\n        area:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/RequestArea'\n        priority:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/RequestPriority'\n        description:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 500\n        id:\n          type: integer\n          format: int64\n          description: Optional caller-supplied value is ignored.\n        createdAt:\n          type: string\n          format: date-time\n          description: Optional caller-supplied value is ignored.\n        status:\n          allOf:\n            - $ref: '#/components/schemas/RequestStatus'\n          description: Optional caller-supplied value is ignored; created requests start Open.\n    ChangeRequestStatus:\n      type: object\n      additionalProperties: false\n      required: [status]\n      properties:\n        status:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/RequestStatus'\n    RequestList:\n      type: object\n      additionalProperties: false\n      required: [requests]\n      properties:\n        requests:\n          type: array\n          items:\n            $ref: '#/components/schemas/MaintenanceRequest'\n    ErrorResponse:\n      type: object\n      additionalProperties: false\n      required: [message]\n      properties:\n        message:\n          type: string\n        errors:\n          type: object\n          description: Field-keyed validation messages when applicable.\n          additionalProperties:\n            type: array\n            items:\n              type: string\n","path":"contracts/openapi.yaml","reason":"Required shared OpenAPI 3.0.3 contract stub for both repositories; excluded from all task file scopes and not implemented in this web-app plan."}],"tasks":[{"approach":"install the packages and build the app once: the scaffold compiles as written","conventions":["Use the factory-generated component kit, theme, frame, navigation, and pages; do not restyle or rebuild generated screens.","Keep the global design tokens in app/globals.css and the shared app shell in app/layout.tsx."],"dependsOn":[],"exemplars":["app/requests/page.tsx","app/requests/[id]/page.tsx"],"fileScope":["app/layout.tsx","package.json","app/globals.css"],"id":"TASK-1","plannedLoc":80,"reqs":["Design-system prerequisite for REQ-22; its screen-level acceptance is completed only after TASK-3."],"title":"Design system and scaffold build"},{"approach":"Wire the existing /requests entry and factory-provided app shell to the Requests container without editing generated route or frame files. Generate the complete typed fetch client from contracts/openapi.yaml into lib/api using the installed OpenAPI generator, then implement list and create behavior in the container. Map API validation errors to field messages; retain values and permit retry after non-validation failure. Do not seed data in the browser: render the API's persisted list, including its initial seeded requests.","conventions":["Treat the factory-generated page and route as immutable; mount behavior through the Requests container's existing integration point.","Use only the contract-generated client in lib/api for list and create calls; do not add fetch calls or a handwritten API client.","Keep list loading, empty, retry, filtering, dialog validation, pending, and failure behavior in this screen slice."],"dependsOn":["TASK-1"],"exemplars":["app/requests/page.tsx","app/requests/[id]/page.tsx"],"fileScope":["components/screens/s-1/container.tsx","lib/api/**"],"id":"TASK-2","plannedLoc":400,"reqs":["REQ-2: render the API resource fields, including system-generated ID and UTC creation timestamp, with description only when present.","REQ-3","REQ-4","REQ-5","REQ-6: display the initial requests provided by the API; seeding and persistence remain API-owned, with no browser-side seeding.","REQ-8","REQ-11","REQ-12","REQ-13","REQ-14","REQ-15","REQ-16","REQ-17"],"title":"Requests screen: live list and create flow"},{"approach":"Connect the existing /requests/[id] route to detail lookup, loading/not-found/error/retry states, and the contract-generated get and status operations. Keep status/action unchanged until success, prevent duplicate submissions while pending, and show the specified failure message on errors. Preserve list filter state on Back. REQ-24 and REQ-25 test artifacts are authored separately because test files are excluded from this scope.","conventions":["Use the generated client created in TASK-2; do not create another API client or edit generated page, layout, or frame files.","Use the existing app navigation and detail route; preserve the selected list filter on Back.","Keep generated design, states, and text intact; supply real API-backed data and behavior from the container."],"dependsOn":["TASK-1","TASK-2"],"exemplars":["app/requests/[id]/page.tsx","components/screens/s-1/container.tsx"],"fileScope":["components/screens/s-2/container.tsx"],"id":"TASK-3","plannedLoc":280,"reqs":["REQ-1","REQ-7","REQ-9","REQ-10","REQ-18","REQ-19","REQ-20","REQ-21","REQ-22","REQ-23","REQ-24","REQ-25"],"title":"Request detail screen: lookup and status transitions"}]}